cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AIFC in research, please cite this repository and the DOI-backed release once available."
title: "AIFC — Auditable Independent-Future Challenge"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Agapov"
    given-names: "Alexander"
    alias: "Hawkar-usls"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-07
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hawkar-usls/AIFC"
url: "https://github.com/Hawkar-usls/AIFC"
abstract: >-
  AIFC is a proof-carrying, adversarial scientific protocol for testing claims
  that exact information about independently generated future random events
  existed before target generation. It composes causal-isolation evidence,
  history-wise conditional entropy, candidate multiplicity accounting,
  anytime-valid sequential inference, external anti-rollback freshness,
  Byzantine-safe witness quorums, and fail-closed evidence grades.
keywords:
  - reproducible research
  - causal inference
  - randomness
  - sequential inference
  - e-process
  - cryptographic provenance
  - scientific methodology
  - retrocausality testing
  - proof-carrying evidence
